# Pull requests

## Branch and scope

- Never commit to `main`. Branch from it, named `type/topic`, matching the history here:
  `fix/library`, `fix/release`, `feat/x-vendor`, `feat/brand`.
- One topic per pull request. A generator fix and a docs rewrite are two pull requests.
- A commit pushed straight to `main` never appears in any release notes, because the
  notes are built from merged pull requests.

## The title is the changelog

`.github/workflows/release.yml` cuts each GitHub Release with
`gh release create --generate-notes`, and those notes are the **titles of the pull
requests merged since the previous release**. Write the title for someone reading the
releases page, not for the diff:

```text
type(scope): summary in the imperative, no trailing period

type   feat | fix | perf | refactor | docs | test | build | ci | chore
scope  zod | valibot | effect | typebox | arktype | ajv | yup | cli | parser | fixtures | docs | ci
```

```text
fix(valibot): emit valid schemas for null and object enum members
feat(zod): support x-stringbool on boolean properties
docs: point Effect Schema links at the v4 documentation
```

## Labels

Apply exactly one: `bug`, `enhancement`, `documentation`, `breaking` or `dependencies`.
`.github/release.yml` groups the generated notes by that label, and anything unlabelled
falls into "Other changes".

## Body

Fill in `.github/pull_request_template.md` rather than replacing it. The section that
matters most here is **Generated output**: this repository's review artifact is the
`fixtures/*/*/output.ts` diff, so paste the interesting part of it or say plainly that
generated output is unchanged.

## Green before you open it

```bash
vp run -r check       # format, lint, types
vp run lint           # Markdown, terminology, spelling, secrets, links
vp test && vp run schema-to-library#test
vp run -r typecheck   # generated code against the real target libraries
```

## A version bump is a release

`release.yml` tags `v<version>`, publishes to npm and creates the GitHub release as soon
as `main` carries a version of `packages/schema-to-library/package.json` that is not on
the registry. Bumping that version **is** the release — never include a bump in a pull
request that was not asked to publish one.

## Opening it

```bash
gh pr create --base main --title 'fix(zod): …' --label bug --body-file <file>
```
